   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription A pharmaceutical company based in Kochi has allegedly been duped of ₹99 lakh by an unidentified fraudster who impersonated the chief executive officer of the firm on WhatsApp. The Kochi City Cyber police have registered a case in connection with the incident based on a complaint. The alleged incident took place on October 16.",
   "summary_zh": "科钦一家制药公司据称被一名冒充公司首席执行官的身份不明诈骗犯通过WhatsApp骗走9900万卢比。科钦市网络警察已根据投诉就此事件立案。所谓事件发生在10月16日。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription A pharmaceutical company based in Kochi has allegedly been duped of ₹99 lakh by an unidentified fraudster who impersonated the chief executive officer of the firm on WhatsApp. The Kochi City Cyber police have registered a case in connection with the incident based on a complaint. The alleged incident took place on October 16. According to the FIR, the accused hacked a mobile phone used by the company’s accounts department and managed to save a phone number as that of the CEO, using the WhatsApp display picture used by him. The fraudster then allegedly communicated with the accounts department staff, posing as the CEO, and convinced a female staffer to transfer the amount to another account. The case has been registered under relevant sections of the IT Act and the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
