   "summary": "The Human Rights Court 2 of the High Court in Accra has temporarily barred the Medical and Dental Council (MDC) from requiring 792 newly trained medical doctors to sit the Stage 1 Common Registration Examination (CRE) before obtaining provisional registration. The injunction also applies to the Attorney-General and the Ministry of Health, preventing them from enforcing the examination requirement until the court hears the substantive case and an application for an injunction on notice.",
   "summary_zh": "阿克拉高等法院人权法庭2庭已临时禁止医疗和牙科委员会（MDC）要求792名新培训的医生在获得临时注册前参加第一阶段共同注册考试（CRE）。该禁令也适用于总检察长和卫生部，阻止他们在法院审理实质案件和通知禁令申请之前执行考试要求。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "The Human Rights Court 2 of the High Court in Accra has temporarily barred the Medical and Dental Council (MDC) from requiring 792 newly trained medical doctors to sit the Stage 1 Common Registration Examination (CRE) before obtaining provisional registration. The injunction also applies to the Attorney-General and the Ministry of Health, preventing them from enforcing the examination requirement until the court hears the substantive case and an application for an injunction on notice. The legal action was brought by the Federation of Ghana Medical Students’ Associations (FGMSA) and the affected students",
