   "summary": "The governor gave the charge on Tuesday when the leadership of the Nigeria Union of Journalists (NUJ), Adamawa State Council, led by its chairman, Comrade Abdullahi Ibrahim, paid him a courtesy visit at Government House, Yola. Earlier, the NUJ chairman, Abdullahi Ibrahim, thanked Fintiri for his continued support for the union, explaining that the visit aimed to strengthen the relationship between the association and the state government.",
   "summary_zh": "州长周二作出指示，当时由主席同志阿卜杜拉希·易卜拉欣率领的尼日利亚记者工会（NUJ）阿达马瓦州理事会领导层前往约拉政府大楼对他进行礼节性拜访。此前，NUJ主席阿卜杜拉希·易卜拉欣感谢芬蒂里对工会的持续支持，并解释说此次访问旨在加强协会与州政府之间的关系。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The governor gave the charge on Tuesday when the leadership of the Nigeria Union of Journalists (NUJ), Adamawa State Council, led by its chairman, Comrade Abdullahi Ibrahim, paid him a courtesy visit at Government House, Yola. Fintiri commended the NUJ for maintaining a cordial relationship with the state government and assured the union that his administration would continue to welcome constructive criticism aimed at advancing the state’s development. He described journalists as the light of society, stressing the media’s important role in promoting peace, development and accountability. The governor also reaffirmed his administration’s commitment to improving the operations and service delivery of the state-owned media organisation. He assured the NUJ leadership that its demands would receive the necessary attention. Earlier, the NUJ chairman, Abdullahi Ibrahim, thanked Fintiri for his continued support for the union, explaining that the visit aimed to strengthen the relationship between the association and the state government. Ibrahim commended the governor for the infrastructural development recorded across the state and for sponsoring some journalists to visit the holy lands to fulfil their religious obligations. He also expressed the union’s support for Fintiri’s senatorial ambition in Adamawa North Senatorial District, where he is seeking a seat in the National Assembly. The NUJ chairman appealed to the governor to facilitate the construction of a secretariat complex for the union in Adamawa State and provide an operational vehicle to support its activities. Highlights of the visit included the appointment of Fintiri as Patron of the NUJ in Adamawa State, the presentation of an award and the presentation of kolanut ahead of the governor’s birthday celebration next week. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
