   "ageDays": 0.74,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The U.S. and India are “pretty close” to making a trade deal, which will be much different than the earlier pacts, U.S. President Donald Trump said in Washington. Speaking to reporters at the Oval Office on Tuesday (October 20, 2026), Mr. Trump said India and the U.S. were pretty close to making a trade deal. USA / India / trade agreements / international (foreign) trade / diplomacy / Donald Trump Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后解锁这些内容 美国和印度“非常接近”达成一项贸易协议，这将与先前的协议有很大不同，美国总统唐纳德·特朗普在华盛顿表示。特朗普先生周二（2026年10月20日）在椭圆形办公室对记者说，印度和美国非常接近达成一项贸易协议。美国/印度/贸易协定/国际（对外）贸易/外交/唐纳德·特朗普 评论必须用英语，并以完整的句子形式。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The U.S. and India are “pretty close” to making a trade deal, which will be much different than the earlier pacts, U.S. President Donald Trump said in Washington. Speaking to reporters at the Oval Office on Tuesday (October 20, 2026), Mr. Trump said India and the U.S. were pretty close to making a trade deal. “They want to make a deal. We're going to make a deal. Pretty close, yeah,” Mr. Trump said in response to a question. “It’s going to be a much different kind of deal than we've done,\" the President said. Mr. Trump’s remarks came at a time Secretary of State Marco Rubio was visiting India and discussed further strengthening bilateral relations focussing on sectors such as trade, energy, technology, defence and people-to-people ties. Earlier this month, Commerce Minister Piyush Goyal met U.S. Trade Representative Jamieson Greer in Milwaukee and Washington to discuss the finer aspects of the trade deal. India and the U.S in February announced the finalisation of the framework for the first phase of the bilateral trade agreement (BTA). However, changes in the tariff landscape in the U.S. have led to further negotiations on the pact. USA / India / trade agreements / international (foreign) trade / diplomacy / Donald Trump Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
