   "title": "T.N. government should construct new Secretariat complex outside Chennai, says Anbumani",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/tamil-nadu/tn-government-should-construct-new-secretariat-complex-outside-chennai-says-anbumani/article71604935.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:04:17 +0530",
   "_dt": 1792550057.0,
   "ageDays": 0.77,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription PMK president Anbumani Ramadoss said on Tuesday (October 20, 2026) that the Tamil Nadu government should look at building the new Secretariat complex outside Chennai as proposed by his party and abandon the plans to build it within city limits. In a statement, he expressed shock over reports that the State government was now considering building the new Secretariat on land occupied by Pallavan Illam on Anna Salai as opposed to an earlier proposal to construct it in Pattinapakkam .",
   "summary_zh": "人民党主席安布马尼·拉马多斯周二（2026年10月20日）表示，泰米尔纳德邦政府应考虑按照其政党提议在金奈以外地区建设新的秘书处大楼，并放弃在市区范围内建设的计划。他在一份声明中对有关邦政府目前正考虑在安娜·萨莱由帕拉万·伊拉姆占用的土地上建设新秘书处的报道表示震惊，此前提议是在帕蒂纳帕卡姆建造。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription PMK president Anbumani Ramadoss said on Tuesday (October 20, 2026) that the Tamil Nadu government should look at building the new Secretariat complex outside Chennai as proposed by his party and abandon the plans to build it within city limits. In a statement, he expressed shock over reports that the State government was now considering building the new Secretariat on land occupied by Pallavan Illam on Anna Salai as opposed to an earlier proposal to construct it in Pattinapakkam . “The Tamil Nadu government must clarify whether the media reports about constructing the Secretariat at Pallavan Illam are true. If there are numerous reasons and justifications for not constructing the new Secretariat in Pattinapakkam, there are a hundred times more compelling reasons for not building it at Pallavan Illam,” he said. According to Dr. Anbumani, the traffic congestion would be impossible to resolve. “If Chennai’s most congested traffic locations were ranked, the area around Pallavan Illam would figure among the top three. Anna Salai, one of Chennai’s principal roads, is already struggling with severe traffic congestion. If the new Secretariat is established at Pallavan Illam, controlling traffic congestion on Anna Salai would become virtually impossible,” he asserted. According to Dr. Anbumani, the entire site at Pallavan Illam measures only 13.22 acres, while the area of the site in Pattinapakkam around 26.36 acres. “During the DMK government led by former Chief Minister M. Karunanidhi, 39.54 acres were earmarked in 2007 for constructing a new Secretariat on Omandurar Government Estate. The land occupied by the buildings originally constructed to house the Secretariat and Legislative Assembly Secretariat, which now accommodate the Omandurar Multi Super Speciality Hospital and medical colleges, measure 19.48 acres,” he said. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "af"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
