   "_dt": 1792539209.0,
   "ageDays": 0.9,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Speaking to The Hindu, several participants of the rally raised concerns about rising criminal activities in the State. Participants also raised concerns about farmers’ plights, unemployment, and rising inflation, stating that the State government and officials had fallen short of supporting the poorest of the poor sections of society and had not delivered on the promises they had made.",
   "summary_zh": "在接受《印度报》采访时，集会上的几名参与者对该邦犯罪活动上升表示担忧。参与者还对农民的困境、失业以及不断上升的通货膨胀表示担忧，他们指出邦政府和官员未能支持社会中最贫困的群体，也没有兑现他们所作的承诺。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Speaking to The Hindu, several participants of the rally raised concerns about rising criminal activities in the State. “It’s happening in Mumbai, it’s happening in Thane. It was Purnekar last month. It was Tiger Shroff yesterday. Tomorrow it will be the common man like you and I,” a party supporter from Jalgaon taluka, who requested anonymity, said. Participants also raised concerns about farmers’ plights, unemployment, and rising inflation, stating that the State government and officials had fallen short of supporting the poorest of the poor sections of society and had not delivered on the promises they had made. Amid rising political dissent against the State and union governments, rally participants said that the party (Shiv Sena-UBT) will continue to support those who stand with the people. “We stand by the cockroaches (Cockroach Janata Party) and officials like Tukaram Mundhe, IAS. The government has let the rich get richer, and the poor remain poor,” said Anil Nagnath Vyavahare, 65, who was attending the rally. Participants also noted that the officials in authority and those in power have still not delivered justice to the students who faced paper leaks in the MPSC, UPSC, and NEET examinations. They said that if the government continues to support gangster activities and tries to manipulate the Indian Constitution and its judiciary, it will soon lose its power, and in the next election, the people will choose those who understand them and stand for their betterment. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
