   "_dt": 1792522800.0,
   "ageDays": 1.09,
   "summary": "Suspected jihadists were behind weekend attacks on camps in northeastern Mali, which killed at least 48 civilians and caused others to flee for their lives, sources told AFP Tuesday. The Daoussahak community is where the armed Movement for the Salvation of Azawad (MSA) originated, a group aligned with Mali's ruling junta, according to security and community sources. Multiple local sources blamed the attack on the Islamic State group's Sahel branch.",
   "summary_zh": "据消息人士周二告诉法新社，疑似圣战分子在周末对马里东北部营地发动袭击，造成至少48名平民死亡，其他人则逃命。道萨哈克社区是与马里执政军政府结盟的阿扎瓦德救世运动（MSA）的发源地，据安全和社区消息人士称。多位当地消息人士将袭击归咎于伊斯兰国组织的萨赫勒分支。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Suspected jihadists were behind weekend attacks on camps in northeastern Mali, which killed at least 48 civilians and caused others to flee for their lives, sources told AFP Tuesday. The attacks hit the restive west African country's Menaka region, where gunmen reportedly rode in on motorcycles and opened fire on camps mainly housing members of the Daoussahak community. The Daoussahak community is where the armed Movement for the Salvation of Azawad (MSA) originated, a group aligned with Mali's ruling junta, according to security and community sources. The death toll from Sunday's attacks, which on Monday stood at more than 40 civilians, has now risen to at least 48 civilians killed, sources said. Another 11 people are missing, a local official told AFP, speaking on condition of anonymity. \"The jihadists threatened to return. There is reason to fear displacement of the population,\" the source said. Multiple local sources blamed the attack on the Islamic State group's Sahel branch. The targeted camps lie about 50 kilometres (30 miles) from the town of Menaka, in or around the village of Tinabow and the Tagadayat area. A security source based in the city of Gao told AFP the massacre occurred \"in retaliation for military operations carried out in the area recently and for attacks by the MSA\". Mali has been plagued since 2012 by a security crisis pitting the army and its Russian allies against jihadist fighters, Tuareg separatist groups and criminal gangs. Since the army took power in back-to-back coups in 2020 and 2021, the ruling junta has turned to Russia for support, enlisting the services of paramilitaries from the Wagner Group, which became the Africa Corps in 2025. Mali's army said it had carried out strikes on Saturday southwest of Menaka targeting \"a major base harbouring terrorist elements and materiel\". The Sahel region has also been hit by recent fighting between Al-Qaeda and IS group factions in the borderlands spanning Burkina Faso, Mali and Niger. Top news and features from AFP's reporters around the world. Page: afp",
