   "_dt": 1792506423.0,
   "ageDays": 1.28,
   "summary": "President Lee Jae Myung on Tuesday stressed the need to cut the time required for administrative procedures in building homes, calling for all-out efforts to boost housing supply. The president made the call during a Cabinet meeting as runaway housing prices persist despite the government's efforts to cool the market.",
   "summary_zh": "李在明总统周二强调需要缩短建造房屋的行政程序所需时间，呼吁全力以赴增加住房供应。总统是在内阁会议上发出这一呼吁的，尽管政府努力冷却市场，但房价仍在失控上涨。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "President Lee Jae Myung on Tuesday stressed the need to cut the time required for administrative procedures in building homes, calling for all-out efforts to boost housing supply. The president made the call during a Cabinet meeting as runaway housing prices persist despite the government's efforts to cool the market. \"Stable housing is the foundation for practical improvements in people's lives,\" Lee said, citing a decline in housing construction permits and the supply of new land for real estate development over the past three years as reasons for disruptions in housing supply. \"In order to resolve the current problems in the real estate market, created by various factors that have accumulated over the years, consistent market management policies and large-scale housing supply measures should be implemented promptly,\" he added. \"I ask you to make all-out efforts with the determination that the success of administrative management depends on stabilizing the housing (market),\" he noted",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
