   "title": "Temple plea for elephant procession: Kerala HC says SC-fixed registration deadline can’t be extended by HC or govt",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/temple-plea-for-elephant-procession-kerala-hc-says-sc-fixed-registration-deadline-cant-be-extended-by-hc-or-govt/article71603853.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:05:55 +0530",
   "_dt": 1792488955.0,
   "ageDays": 1.48,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Neither the High Court nor the State government can extend the timeline fixed by the Supreme Court for temples and devaswoms to register with the District Committee constituted under the Kerala Captive Elephant (Management and Maintenance) Rules, 2012, the Kerala High Court has observed.",
   "summary_zh": "高等法院和州政府都不能延长最高法院为寺庙和 devaswoms 向根据 2012 年喀拉拉邦圈养大象（管理和维护）规则设立的地区委员会登记所确定的时间表，喀拉拉邦高等法院表示。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Neither the High Court nor the State government can extend the timeline fixed by the Supreme Court for temples and devaswoms to register with the District Committee constituted under the Kerala Captive Elephant (Management and Maintenance) Rules, 2012, the Kerala High Court has observed. Justice Bechu Kurian Thomas opined that without any extension of the time granted by the Supreme Court, it was not proper for the High Court to direct a delayed registration or even to direct the consideration of an application for time extension. The court was considering a petition by the trustee and the president of the Sree Manathala Shiva-Parvathi Temple seeking a direction to register the temple under the District Committee and to grant permission to conduct elephant procession in connection with the temple festival. The Supreme Court had directed that temples or devaswoms should register themselves with the District Committee within six weeks from August 18, 2015. The government issued an order in April 2022 permitting registration of elephant parades, for the strict implementation of the apex court’s directives. The petitioners argued that they had paraded elephants for several years and continued to do so during festivals even after the rules were enacted. They stated that they could not register the temple within the extended time and that they preferred to apply to the Minister of Forests, Keralam, for registration, but their application was denied. The petitioners further argued that the Supreme Court had only directed the implementation of the rules and did not strictly stipulate a time limit. They also contended that ‘a sympathetic consideration’ of the matter would not cause prejudice to anyone. The Assistant Conservator of Forests pointed out that they received 84 applications during the extended time, and despite the grant of several opportunities, the petitioner’s temple had not filed any application. The court maintained that though the Supreme Court held that registration of the temple or the devaswom was necessary for effective and proper control, the timeline fixed therein is only six weeks from August 2015. A purpose was evident from the timeline fixed, the court observed. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "af"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_thehindu",
   "title_zh": "寺庙为大象游行请愿：喀拉拉邦高等法院称最高法院确定的登记截止日期不能由高等法院或政府延长",
   "body_zh": "订阅账户福利以及高级故事、社论、观点等。使用订阅解锁这些内容。喀拉拉邦高等法院指出，高等法院或邦政府均不能延长最高法院为寺庙和德瓦斯沃姆机构规定的与根据 2012 年《喀拉拉邦圈养大象（管理和维护）规则》设立的地区委员会进行登记的期限。大法官贝丘·库里安·托马斯认为，在没有最高法院准予延期的情况下，高等法院指示延迟登记或甚至指示考虑延期申请是不适当的。法院正在审理 Sree Manathala Shiva-Parvathi Temple 信托人兼主席提出的一项请愿书，该请愿书寻求指示将该寺庙在地区委员会下登记，并准许在寺庙节日期间进行大象游行。最高法院曾指示寺庙或德瓦斯沃姆机构应在 2015 年 8 月 18 日起六周内向地区委员会登记。政府于 2022 年 4 月发布命令，允许登记大象游行，以严格执行最高法院的指示。请愿者辩称，他们多年来一直进行大象游行，即使在规则颁布后，在节日期间也继续这样做。他们表示，他们无法在延长期限内登记寺庙，他们倾向于向喀拉拉姆森林部长申请登记，但他们的申请被拒绝。请愿者进一步辩称，最高法院只是指示执行这些规则，并没有严格规定时间限制。他们还争辩说，对此事进行‘同情考虑’不会对任何人造成损害。森林助理保护官指出，他们在延长期限内收到了 84 份申请，尽管给予了多次机会，请愿者的寺庙仍未提交任何申请。法院坚持认为，尽管最高法院认为寺庙或德瓦斯沃姆机构的登记对于有效和适当的控制是必要的，但其中规定的时间表仅为 2015 年 8 月起的六周。法院指出，从规定的时间表中可以看出一个目的。评论必须用英语，并使用完整句子。它们不能是辱骂性的或涉及个人的。请遵守我们发布评论的社区准则。我们已迁移到新的评论平台。如果您已经是《印度教徒报》的注册用户并已登录，您可以继续与我们的文章互动。如果您没有账户，请注册并登录以发布评论。用户可以通过登录他们在 Vuukle 上的账户来访问他们以前的评论。",
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": ""
