   "platform": "x",
   "title": "Norwegian authorities reportedly detained two Chinese cargo ships on October 14.",
   "url": "https://x.com/Gerashchenko_en/status/2112502993010438260",
   "snippet": "Norwegian authorities reportedly detained two Chinese cargo ships on October 14. One of them, Ya Qing Hai Yang, is under sanctions for its links to Arctic LNG 2, a Russian natural gas project on the Gydan Peninsula.\n\nAccording to Starboard Maritime Intelligence, the vessel was spotted near the Norwegian border in early October. Flying the Guatemalan flag, it had sailed from Hong Kong via the Northern Sea Route, making several stops in the Far East.\n\nIn 2024, Ya Qing Hai Yang transported power generation modules from China to Russia's Utrenny port, which serves the Arctic LNG 2 project. The shipment led to the vessel being sanctioned by the U.S., EU, and Switzerland.\n\nThe second vessel, Jian Yang Cheng He, is not under sanctions, and no links to Russian projects have been reported.\n\nAccording to the Norwegian Coast Guard, the vessels had sought shelter from a storm near Andøya Island in northern Norway. Coast Guard personnel conducted an inspection.\n\nBoth vessels reportedly remain off the Norwegian coast.",
   "body": "Norwegian authorities reportedly detained two Chinese cargo ships on October 14. One of them, Ya Qing Hai Yang, is under sanctions for its links to Arctic LNG 2, a Russian natural gas project on the Gydan Peninsula.\n\nAccording to Starboard Maritime Intelligence, the vessel was spotted near the Norwegian border in early October. Flying the Guatemalan flag, it had sailed from Hong Kong via the Northern Sea Route, making several stops in the Far East.\n\nIn 2024, Ya Qing Hai Yang transported power generation modules from China to Russia's Utrenny port, which serves the Arctic LNG 2 project. The shipment led to the vessel being sanctioned by the U.S., EU, and Switzerland.\n\nThe second vessel, Jian Yang Cheng He, is not under sanctions, and no links to Russian projects have been reported.\n\nAccording to the Norwegian Coast Guard, the vessels had sought shelter from a storm near Andøya Island in northern Norway. Coast Guard personnel conducted an inspection.\n\nBoth vessels reportedly remain off the Norwegian coast.",
