   "title": "Ladakh is not China. Tibet is not China’s property to control. Ladakh’s Apex Body has firmly rejected Beijing’s latest claim over Ladakh, de",
   "url": "https://x.com/dc4_humanrights/status/2112436906159997097",
   "snippet": "Ladakh is not China. Tibet is not China’s property to control. \n\nLadakh’s Apex Body has firmly rejected Beijing’s latest claim over Ladakh, declaring that the region was never part of China. Its representatives also pointed to a painful reality: China’s forced exile of His Holiness the Dalai Lama remains a deep wound for Ladakhis, who share close cultural, religious and historical ties with Tibet.\n\nFor decades, the CCP has sought to tighten its grip on Tibet, restricting religious freedom, suppressing Tibetan identity and attempting to control the Dalai Lama’s succession. Now Beijing’s territorial claims are being challenged by people who refuse to let their history be rewritten.\n\nBorders cannot be rewritten by propaganda, and a people’s identity cannot be erased by political decree. Tibetans and Ladakhis deserve respect for their history, culture and right to preserve their heritage.\n\n#Ladakh #Tibet #FreeTibet #India #China #CCP #DalaiLama #StandWithTibet #TibetanRights #LadakhIsNotChina #TibetIsNotChina #HumanRights #ReligiousFreedom #Himalayas #StopForcedAssimilation",
   "body": "Ladakh is not China. Tibet is not China’s property to control. \n\nLadakh’s Apex Body has firmly rejected Beijing’s latest claim over Ladakh, declaring that the region was never part of China. Its representatives also pointed to a painful reality: China’s forced exile of His Holiness the Dalai Lama remains a deep wound for Ladakhis, who share close cultural, religious and historical ties with Tibet.\n\nFor decades, the CCP has sought to tighten its grip on Tibet, restricting religious freedom, suppressing Tibetan identity and attempting to control the Dalai Lama’s succession. Now Beijing’s territorial claims are being challenged by people who refuse to let their history be rewritten.\n\nBorders cannot be rewritten by propaganda, and a people’s identity cannot be erased by political decree. Tibetans and Ladakhis deserve respect for their history, culture and right to preserve their heritage.\n\n#Ladakh #Tibet #FreeTibet #India #China #CCP #DalaiLama #StandWithTibet #TibetanRights #LadakhIsNotChina #TibetIsNotChina #HumanRights #ReligiousFreedom #Himalayas #StopForcedAssimilation",
