   "url": "https://x.com/thecableng/status/2112273664414765438",
   "snippet": "Burkina Faso, Niger, Mali, resume talks with ECOWAS — 18 months after withdrawal\n\nBurkina Faso, Niger Republic and Mali have resumed talks with the Economic Community of West African States (ECOWAS), more than 18 months after the three countries withdrew from the regional bloc.\n\nThe two sides agreed on Saturday to establish joint working groups to develop a framework agreement for cooperation.\n\nThe three countries, led by military juntas withdrew from ECOWAS in January 2025 after forming the Alliance of Sahel States (AES), following a series of military coups and tensions with the regional bloc.",
   "body": "Burkina Faso, Niger, Mali, resume talks with ECOWAS — 18 months after withdrawal\n\nBurkina Faso, Niger Republic and Mali have resumed talks with the Economic Community of West African States (ECOWAS), more than 18 months after the three countries withdrew from the regional bloc.\n\nThe two sides agreed on Saturday to establish joint working groups to develop a framework agreement for cooperation.\n\nThe three countries, led by military juntas withdrew from ECOWAS in January 2025 after forming the Alliance of Sahel States (AES), following a series of military coups and tensions with the regional bloc.",
